---
/**
 * /terms — Terms and Conditions (SMS messaging programs scope).
 *
 * Updated 2026-05-23: dual-program restructure to support the second
 * SignalWire/TCR campaign registration (marketing/loyalty). Major changes:
 *   - Section 2 split: Program A (Event Inquiry & Information,
 *     transactional) + Program B (Marketing & Loyalty, promotional)
 *   - Section 3 expanded to six opt-in paths (a–f): the two existing
 *     event-inquiry paths plus four new marketing paths (signup form,
 *     keyword opt-in, in-venue enrollment, prior-provider subscribers)
 *   - Section 4 frequency split per program (Program B ≤8/month)
 *   - Section 6 opt-out clarified as per-program (opting out of one
 *     doesn't opt you out of the other)
 *   - Section 8 broadened to cover both programs
 *   - Added /sms-marketing as a parallel program disclosure page
 *
 * Updated 2026-05-08: substantive rewrite to support SMS messaging
 * program approval. Major additions:
 *   - Dow Holdings Inc named as the operating legal entity
 *   - Section 3(b): verbal phone opt-in path documented in detail —
 *     AI receptionist offers to send info via text, single SMS sent on
 *     verbal confirmation, consent logged with timestamp + recording
 *   - Section 2: informational link messages added to program scope
 *   - Section 8: CTIA-mandated "no mobile sharing" boilerplate
 *   - Re-enroll path now includes verbal phone request
 *
 * The live page is scoped to the SMS messaging programs (TCPA / CTIA
 * compliance scaffold) PLUS, as of 2026-08-31, Section 10: the
 * cancellation terms for event bookings. Jon explicitly declined a
 * counsel pass ("pluck the low-hanging fruit in terms of coverage and
 * call it a day") — these are the same operative sentences the TPRS pay
 * page, booking emails and /faq state, so a wording change on any of
 * those surfaces should be mirrored here.
 *
 * SUPERSEDED 2026-09-05: the 8/31 ruling had TWO rails (catered
 * refundable until final payment; a flat 72 hours for everything paid
 * in full at booking). There are FOUR. Kids birthday packages moved to
 * their own 14-day rule, and NYE to its own no-refund rule, so the
 * single pay-in-full paragraph became three. Full rationale sits on the
 * Section 10 block below. The discretion clause is unchanged and is
 * what lets Jon be generous — he notes we have never actually failed to
 * refund or issue a gift card on NYE — without the courtesy rewriting
 * the stated term.
 *
 * Structural note: if a full website-use ToS is ever needed (gift card
 * terms, prize / promotion rules, governing law, liability
 * disclaimers), it should either:
 *   (a) live on a separate /terms-of-use page and link to here, OR
 *   (b) replace this page with a comprehensive ToS that retains the
 *       SMS sections at the back
 */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import SnapFooter from "../components/snap/SnapFooter.astro";
import BreadcrumbSchema from "../components/BreadcrumbSchema.astro";

const LAST_UPDATED = "September 5, 2026";
---
<Base
  title="Terms and Conditions | Twisted Pin"
  description="Terms and Conditions for Twisted Pin's SMS messaging programs — opt-in, opt-out, message frequency, eligibility, contact info. Plainfield, IL."
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex,follow" />
  </Fragment>

  <section class="t2-hero" data-hero aria-labelledby="terms-h1">
    <div class="t2-hero-copy">
      <p class="t-eyebrow hero-fade" data-delay-ms="0">Twisted Pin · SMS Messaging Programs</p>
      <h1 class="t-display t2-hero-headline hero-fade" id="terms-h1" data-delay-ms="120">
        Terms &amp; Conditions.
      </h1>
      <p class="t2-hero-sub hero-fade" data-delay-ms="320">
        Last updated {LAST_UPDATED}. The terms below govern both
        Twisted Pin SMS messaging programs — the transactional/event
        inquiry program and the marketing/loyalty program — and the
        cancellation terms for reservations and event
        bookings (Section 10). By opting in to either SMS program via
        any of the consent paths described in Section 3, you agree to
        these terms.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="t2-section legal-section" aria-labelledby="terms-h2-1">
    <div class="t2-section-inner">
      <h2 class="legal-h2" id="terms-h2-1">1. Overview</h2>
      <p>These Terms and Conditions govern your use of the Twisted Pin SMS messaging programs, operated by Dow Holdings Inc. By opting in to either program via any of the consent paths described in Section 3 below, you agree to these terms. Please read them carefully before participating.</p>

      <h2 class="legal-h2" id="terms-h2-2">2. Program Description</h2>
      <p>Twisted Pin ("Twisted Pin," "we," "us"), a brand operated by Dow Holdings Inc, operates two distinct opt-in SMS messaging programs:</p>

      <h3 class="legal-h3">Program A: Event Inquiry &amp; Information (transactional)</h3>
      <p>Messages sent in response to a customer-initiated inquiry or information request. Program A messages may include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Responses to event booking inquiries</li>
        <li>Custom event quotes and pricing information</li>
        <li>Availability confirmations and booking details</li>
        <li>Informational links sent in response to phone inquiries (pricing, hours, directions, location)</li>
        <li>Customer service follow-up related to your event</li>
        <li>Event reminders and confirmations</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="legal-h3">Program B: Marketing &amp; Loyalty (promotional)</h3>
      <p>Recurring promotional messages sent to customers who have explicitly opted in. Program B messages may include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Promotional offers and discounts</li>
        <li>Event announcements (holidays, themed nights, special programming)</li>
        <li>Loyalty program notifications, including Insider tier perks</li>
        <li>Birthday and anniversary rewards</li>
        <li>Seasonal campaigns and venue news</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="legal-h2" id="terms-h2-3">3. How to Opt In</h2>

      <h3 class="legal-h3">Program A opt-in paths</h3>
      <p><strong>(a) Web form opt-in:</strong> By submitting your phone number through our event inquiry form at twistedpin.com. By providing your phone number and submitting the form, you expressly consent to receive text messages from Twisted Pin at the number provided.</p>
      <p><strong>(b) Verbal opt-in:</strong> By verbally requesting that information be sent to you via text message during a phone call to our business line at 815-782-7790. When you call and ask for details such as pricing, hours, directions, or location, our AI receptionist will offer to send the information via text. If you verbally confirm, a single informational SMS will be sent to the phone number from which you are calling. Verbal consent is captured and logged with date, timestamp, and call recording.</p>

      <h3 class="legal-h3">Program B opt-in paths</h3>
      <p><strong>(c) Marketing signup form:</strong> By submitting your phone number through a signup form on our website (such as twistedpin.com/signup) and checking the marketing-consent checkbox, you expressly consent to receive recurring promotional text messages from Twisted Pin at the number provided.</p>
      <p><strong>(d) Keyword opt-in:</strong> By texting an opt-in keyword (such as BOWL or KIDS) to our marketing number. We send a confirmation message restating the program terms after a keyword opt-in.</p>
      <p><strong>(e) In-venue enrollment:</strong> By signing up at our in-venue kiosk and providing explicit consent. Consent is captured with timestamp and source.</p>
      <p><strong>(f) Existing subscribers:</strong> Customers who previously opted in to Twisted Pin SMS marketing through our prior SMS provider remain enrolled under these terms. Consent records are preserved through the migration. Anyone wishing to opt out can do so at any time per Section 6.</p>

      <p>In all cases, you confirm that you are the account holder of the mobile number provided, or have the account holder's permission to enroll.</p>

      <h2 class="legal-h2" id="terms-h2-4">4. Message Frequency</h2>
      <p><strong>Program A (Event Inquiry &amp; Information):</strong> Frequency varies based on your inquiry. For event inquiry opt-ins, you may receive multiple messages per inquiry as we assist you with quotes, availability, and booking details. For verbal phone opt-ins, you will typically receive a single informational message per request.</p>
      <p><strong>Program B (Marketing &amp; Loyalty):</strong> Frequency varies based on the season and campaigns we are running, but typically does not exceed eight (8) messages per month per subscriber.</p>

      <h2 class="legal-h2" id="terms-h2-5">5. Message and Data Rates</h2>
      <p>Message and data rates may apply. These charges are billed by your mobile carrier and are not collected by Twisted Pin. Please contact your mobile carrier if you are unsure about your messaging and data plan rates.</p>

      <h2 class="legal-h2" id="terms-h2-6">6. How to Opt Out (STOP)</h2>
      <p>You may opt out of receiving SMS messages from Twisted Pin at any time by replying <strong>STOP</strong> to any message you receive from us.</p>
      <p>After texting STOP, you will receive one final confirmation message and no further messages will be sent from that program. Opting out of one program does not opt you out of the other — if you are enrolled in both Program A and Program B, reply STOP to a message in each program you wish to leave.</p>
      <p>To re-enroll, use any of the opt-in paths described in Section 3 for the program you wish to rejoin.</p>
      <p>Other opt-out keywords we honor: STOPALL, UNSUBSCRIBE, CANCEL, END, QUIT.</p>

      <h2 class="legal-h2" id="terms-h2-7">7. How to Get Help (HELP)</h2>
      <p>For help or more information, reply <strong>HELP</strong> to any message or contact us directly at:</p>
      <ul class="legal-contact">
        <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:contactus@twistedpin.com">contactus@twistedpin.com</a></li>
        <li><strong>Phone:</strong> 815-782-7790</li>
        <li><strong>Address:</strong> Twisted Pin, 15610 Joliet Rd, Plainfield, IL 60544</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="legal-h2" id="terms-h2-8">8. Privacy</h2>
      <p>Your phone number and personal information collected through our SMS programs will be used solely to deliver the program you opted into — responding to inquiries and fulfilling information requests under Program A, and delivering promotional offers and loyalty notifications under Program B. No mobile information will be shared with third parties or affiliates for marketing or promotional purposes. For full details on how we collect and use your data, please review our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>. For the per-program service descriptions, see <a href="/sms/">SMS Information Service</a> (Program A) and <a href="/sms-marketing/">Marketing SMS Program</a> (Program B).</p>

      <h2 class="legal-h2" id="terms-h2-9">9. Eligibility</h2>
      <p>Both SMS programs are available to users with a valid mobile phone number in the United States. By opting in, you represent that you are 18 years of age or older and are the account holder of the mobile number provided, or have authorization from the account holder to enroll.</p>

      {/* Event booking terms (2026-08-31, owner ruling — no counsel pass by
          Jon's explicit call; plain-language coverage is the goal). These are
          the SAME operative sentences the payment page, booking emails and FAQ
          state, transcribed rather than re-invented — the drift risk lives in
          paraphrase. The discretion clause is load-bearing: Jon will refund a
          pushed-to-shove late cancellation as a courtesy, and this lets him do
          that without the exception rewriting the rule.

          2026-09-05 (owner ruling): the single pay-in-full paragraph SPLIT into
          three, because there are FOUR rails, not two, and they differ:
            A Catered (product codes 14/15/16/17 = Pizza & Pop, Stars & Strikes,
              Twisted Italiano, Burrito Bowl): 50% deposit, balance at seven
              days. The ONLY rail where "deposit" and "final payment" may be
              said — Jon: "Those don't and shouldn't produce any final payment
              language terminology because the final payment is made when they
              book online."
            B Kids birthday (109/118, twistedpin.com/kb): paid in full, 14 days,
              move OR refund at the guest's choice. The refund is UNCONDITIONAL
              at 14+ days — never "may be eligible" or "case-by-case" — and the
              date move is deliberately UNBOUNDED (the two-month bound from the
              Roller-era policy was offered on 2026-09-05 and declined).
            C Lane reservations (4/5/121/123): paid in full, 72 hours. Unchanged.
            D NYE (124/126): paid in full, NO refunds, gift certificate at 14+
              days less the service fee. This transcribes the required checkbox
              already live on both TPRS NYE forms (form_fields display_order 5,
              "No refunds!") — the FORMS were right and this page was wrong, so
              an NYE guest was ticking two contradictory required boxes.
          Why B and C differ at all: lane products carry
          max_advance_booking_days = 10, so a 14-day rule is arithmetically
          impossible there. Kids parties open at a 7-day minimum lead
          (sales_cutoff_minutes_before = 10080) with no ceiling, so a party
          booked 7 to 13 days out is past the 14-day line at purchase — Jon
          ruled "leave it, say it plainly" rather than move the cutoff.
          The catered timing says SEVEN DAYS to guests (Jon, 2026-09-05: "we
          request your final headcount seven days prior. Once that's confirmed,
          we request your final payment"). The day-6 check is an INTERNAL
          backstop that triggers Needs Attention; it never appears here. Seven
          and six are not in conflict — we ask a day before it is due, which is
          why the dated deadline on the deposit emails (2026-08-11) still
          stands. */}
      <h2 class="legal-h2" id="terms-h2-10">10. Event Deposits &amp; Cancellations</h2>
      <p>The terms in this section apply to reservations and event bookings made with Twisted Pin.</p>
      <p><strong>Catered events.</strong> A catered event is confirmed with a 50% deposit. Seven days before the event date, Twisted Pin requests the final guest count; once that count is confirmed, the total is updated to reflect it and the remaining balance (the &ldquo;final payment&rdquo;) is requested. A catered event cancelled at any time <strong>before the final payment is collected</strong> receives a full refund of the deposit. Once the final payment has been collected, all payments for the event are final and non-refundable. Date changes requested before the final payment is collected are accommodated at no charge, subject to availability.</p>
      <p><strong>Lane reservations and other bookings paid in full at booking</strong> (other than the online kids birthday party packages and New Year&rsquo;s Eve reservations, each covered below): cancellations must be made at least 72 hours before the reservation to avoid forfeiting payment. Within 72 hours of the reservation, payment is final.</p>
      <p><strong>Online kids birthday party packages.</strong> These packages are paid in full at the time of booking. There is no deposit and no separate later payment. A party cancelled 14 or more days before the party date may be moved to another available date, or refunded in full, at the guest&rsquo;s choice. Within 14 days of the party date, payment is final. Because these packages can be booked as few as seven days ahead, a party booked fewer than 14 days before the party date is final at the time of purchase.</p>
      <p><strong>New Year&rsquo;s Eve reservations.</strong> These reservations are paid in full at the time of booking and are not refundable. If you contact Twisted Pin 14 or more days before the event, a gift certificate will be issued for the reservation amount, less the service fee. Cancellations within 14 days of the event forfeit payment.</p>
      <p><strong>Exceptions.</strong> Twisted Pin may, at its sole discretion, offer a refund, credit, or date change outside these terms. Any such accommodation is a courtesy and does not modify these terms or create an entitlement to future exceptions.</p>

      <h2 class="legal-h2" id="terms-h2-11">11. Changes to These Terms</h2>
      <p>Twisted Pin reserves the right to modify these Terms and Conditions at any time. Changes will be posted at twistedpin.com/terms/. Continued participation in either SMS program, and any booking made after changes are posted, constitutes your acceptance of the updated terms.</p>

      <h2 class="legal-h2" id="terms-h2-12">12. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>If you have questions about these Terms and Conditions or our SMS programs, please contact us:</p>
      <ul class="legal-contact">
        <li><strong>Twisted Pin (operated by Dow Holdings Inc)</strong></li>
        <li>15610 Joliet Rd, Plainfield, IL 60544</li>
        <li><a href="mailto:contactus@twistedpin.com">contactus@twistedpin.com</a></li>
        <li><a href="/">twistedpin.com</a></li>
      </ul>

      <p class="legal-jurisdiction">Twisted Pin is located in Plainfield, Illinois and serves the greater Chicagoland area. Our SMS programs are operated in compliance with TCPA regulations and CTIA messaging guidelines.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SnapFooter />
  <BreadcrumbSchema crumbs={[
    { name: "Home", path: "/" },
    { name: "Terms", path: "/terms/" },
  ]} />
</Base>

<style>
  /* Same legal-page recipe as /privacy — see that file for the
     vocabulary. Hoist to global.css if a third legal page lands. */
  .legal-section .t2-section-inner {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .legal-h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 900;
    font-size: 22px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    color: var(--warm-white);
    margin: 40px 0 14px;
  }
  .legal-h2:first-child { margin-top: 8px; }
  @media (min-width: 760px) {
    .legal-h2 { font-size: 26px; margin-top: 48px; }
  }

  /* H3 sub-sections within an H2 (e.g. "Program A opt-in paths" /
     "Program B opt-in paths" under section 3). Smaller register than
     H2 to read as a sub-divider, not a parallel section. */
  .legal-h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 14px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--warm-white);
    margin: 22px 0 10px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 760px) {
    .legal-h3 { font-size: 15px; }
  }

  .legal-section p,
  .legal-section li {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--warm-mid);
  }
  .legal-section p { margin: 0 0 14px; }

  .legal-section ul {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    padding-left: 22px;
  }
  .legal-section li { margin-bottom: 6px; }

  .legal-section strong { color: var(--warm-white); font-weight: 700; }

  .legal-section a {
    color: var(--glow);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .legal-contact {
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 0;
  }

  .legal-jurisdiction {
    margin-top: 32px;
    padding-top: 20px;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(244, 239, 227, 0.10);
    font-size: 13px !important;
    color: var(--warm-dim) !important;
    font-style: italic;
  }
</style>
